{
 "prompt": "Name a kind of cake",
 "rules": [
  "A thing fits if a fair-minded US player would agree it is a kind of cake: sweet, baked or chilled, cake-like crumb or layered, or called a cake in ordinary US speech.",
  "Bare flavours count as short forms for flavour cakes (chocolate, vanilla, red velvet, lemon, carrot, strawberry); bare rose is borderline.",
  "Cheesecake: accept (universally called a cake). Tiramisu and Boston cream pie: accept as borderline. Cupcake: accept.",
  "Griddle or fried batter foods are NOT cakes even when the word cake appears: pancake, hotcake, johnnycake, funnel cake, crab cake, fish cake, rice cake, potato cake, urinal cake, cake donut.",
  "Brownies, doughnuts, cookies, bars, waffles, fritters, crepes, biscuits, macaroons, shortbread: not cakes; remove.",
  "Branded snack cakes (Twinkie, Ding Dong, Ho Hos): borderline, accepted because sold and called snack cakes; generic snack cake accepted.",
  "Pastries or yeast breads that Wikipedia lists as cakes (babka, panettone, pavlova, mooncake, mille-feuille, madeleine): borderline; accept the well known ones, flagged.",
  "Shape, method and occasion answers count: bundt, sheet, layer, loaf, ice cream, birthday, wedding, anniversary.",
  "Generic words torte and gateau: accept. Quick breads (banana bread, zucchini bread) are not accepted unless the player says cake."
 ],
